nstants: 1 (`5`, now bound to `PROCESSING_FEE`) = 1\n- Bindings: 2 (`_scenario` param, `PROCESSING_FEE`) = 2\n- Invocations: 0 = 0\n- Conditionals: 0 = 0\n- Loops: 0 = 0\n- Assignments: 0 = 0\n\n**Total Mass: 3**\n\nMass Change: 2 → 3 (delta +1)\n\n**Documented rationale**: Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) outranks APP mass minimization. The +1 mass from introducing the `PROCESSING_FEE` binding is justified because it turns an opaque literal into self-documenting domain vocabulary that will remain meaningful as more premium-calculation logic (base premiums, surcharges, discounts) is added around it in later cycles — at which point disambiguating \"the flat fee\" from other numeric constants becomes essential. I considered other refactorings (Rule 3 duplication, Rule 4 fewest elements) but with only one passing test there's no duplication to remove and no unnecessary abstraction to strip — the implementation is otherwise minimal.\n\n---\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted magic number `5` into a named constant `PROCESSING_FEE` (Rule 2 — Reveals Intent)\n**Mass Change**: 2 → 3 (+1, justified by clarity per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All passing (1 passed, 34 todo)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 1\nRecent Green phase: Implemented runScenario to hardcode return { results: [{ premium: 5 }] } for the empty-item-list quote test.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Note: run tests with `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` since NODE_ENV=production is set in the environment by default and prevents vitest devDependency install/run.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type"