# Refactoring Applied\n\nReplaced the manual accumulator loop with `Array.from(...).reduce(...)`, eliminating the mutable `total` binding and its assignment/increment, expressing the sum declaratively.\n\n```ts\nreturn Array.from(countsByType.values()).reduce(\n  (total, count) =>\n    total +\n    (count === 3 ? BLOCK_OF_THREE_PREMIUM : count * BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM),\n  0,\n);\n```\n\n## APP Mass — After Refactoring\n\n- Bindings: `countsByType`, `item`, `total`, `count` = 4 (reduce's `total`/`count` are params, still bindings)\n- Constants: `1` (increment in first loop), `0` (reduce initial) = 2\n- Invocations: `Map` ctor, `.set`, `.get`, `Array.from`, `.values`, `.reduce` = 6\n- Conditionals: 1 (ternary)\n- Loops: 2 (the `for..of` populating the map, and `.reduce` as iteration)\n- Assignments: `countsByType.set(...)` = 1 (no more `total =`/`total +=` statements — reduce's return isn't a mutation)\n\nMass = constants(2×1) + bindings(4×1) + invocations(6×2) + conditionals(1×4) + loops(2×5) + assignments(1×6)\n= 2 + 4 + 12 + 4 + 10 + 6 = **38**\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Replaced imperative `let total` accumulator loop with a `reduce` expression to remove the mutable variable and its assignment statements, improving Rule 2 (intent: \"sum derived values\" reads more directly) and Rule 4 (fewer stateful elements).\n**Naming**: Kept `calculateItemsBasePremium` — already accurately reveals intent.\n**Mass Change**: 46 → 38 (Δ −8), driven by removing 2 assignments at the cost of 2 more invocations (`Array.from`, `.reduce`), a net win since assignments are weighted heaviest.\n**Tests**: All 6 tests passing, no regressions."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-of