(items, policyBase, withFirstInsurance, isLongStanding, withLoyalty, premium) = 6\n- Invocations: 2 (calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers, roundInMhpcoFavorForPremium) = 4\n- Conditionals: 2 (`if`, ternary) = 8\n- Constants: 4 (1, 1, FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE ref counted as binding, but literal `1`s ×2, LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ref, PROCESSING_FEE ref) — counting only literals: `1` appears twice = 2\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass (approx): 6 + 4 + 8 + 2 = **20**\n\n**Rule Evaluation**:\n- Rule 1 (Tests Pass): All 9 tests green before and after — confirmed.\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent): The quote-premium calculation was an anonymous inline block mixed with step-dispatch/mapping concerns inside `runScenario`. Extracting it as `calculateQuotePremium(customer, items)` gives this multi-step business calculation its own name and signature, making `runScenario`'s `.map()` callback read as pure dispatch (\"if quote, get quote premium; else stub claim\").\n- Rule 3 (No Duplication): No duplication found elsewhere in the file.\n- Rule 4 (Fewest Elements): No unnecessary elements added — the extraction is a straight lift with no new abstractions beyond the one function needed for naming clarity.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```ts\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (customer: Customer, items: ItemInput[]): number => {\n  const policyBase = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance = policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const isLongStanding = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n  const withLoyalty = isLongStanding\n    ? withFirstInsurance * (1 - LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE)\n    : withFirstInsurance;\n  return roundInMhpcoFavorForPremium(withLoyalty + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n```\nplus in `runScenario`:\n```ts\nif (step.op === \"quote\") {\n  const premium = calculateQuotePremium(scenario.customer, step.items as ItemInput[]);\n  return { premium };\n}\n```\nMass is essentially unchanged (same operations, just relocated) — 1 extra invocation (call site) but 1 fewer binding (`items` inlined into the call). Net mass ≈ 20 (unchanged).\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Naming: Extracted `calculateQuotePremium` to name the quote-premium calculation explicitly; `runScenario` name retained as it correctly describes the dispatch role.\n- Mass: Essentially unchanged (~20 → ~20) — this refactor targets Rule 2 (clarity), which is prioritized over Rule 4 (mass minimization).\n- Rule 2: `runScenario`'s step-mapping logic is now much easier to scan; the quote calculation is independently testable/readable under its own descriptive name and signature `(customer, items)`.\n\n**Tests**: All 9 passing (26 `it.todo` still pending as expected)."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":7238,"output":1791,"cacheRead":10118,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":19147,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784911747135,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-bffc63f6-dfa3-483c-90bf-df6f42ff0598","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":40932,"output":11025,"cacheRead":49866,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":19147,"turns":6},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784911763785},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01NYiA9kMpAfQ2yKurzhRHoV","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && NODE_ENV=development pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -15 && cat src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":3442,"output":149,"cacheRead":65494,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":69085,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784911763786,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-c7cd6151-ac6d-41fb-8f78-fb2b4dda6a95","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01NYiA9kMpAfQ2yKurzhRHoV","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (35 tests | 26 skipped) 3ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  9 passed | 26 todo (35)\n   Start at  16:49:27\n   Duration  171ms (transform 30ms, setup 0ms, collect 31ms, tests 3ms, environment 0ms, prepare 50ms)\n\nexport interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: unknown[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: unknown;\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport type StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nexport interface ScenarioResult {\n  results: StepResult[];\n}\n\nexport interface ItemInput {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM = 25;\nconst BLOCK_OF_THREE_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nexport const calculateItemsBasePremium = (items: ItemInput[]): number => {\n  const countsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    countsByType.set(item.type, (countsByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n\n  return Array.from(countsByType.values()).reduce(\n    (total, count) =>\n      total +\n      (count === 3 ? BLOCK_OF_THREE_PREMIUM : count * BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM),\n    0,\n  );\n};\n\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst calculateItemPremiumWithCurseModifier = (item: ItemInput): number => {\n  const itemBase = MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? itemBase * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  return itemBase + curseSurcharge;\n};\n\nexport const calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers = (\n  items: ItemInput[],\n): number => {\n  return items.reduce(\n    (total, item) => total + calculateItemPremiumWithCurseModifier(item),\n    0,\n  );\n};\n\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst roundInMhpcoFavorForPremium = (amount: number): number =>\n  Math.ceil(amount);\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: ItemInput[],\n): number => {\n  const policyBase = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance =\n    policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const isLongStanding = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n  const withLoyalty = isLongStanding\n    ? withFirstInsurance * (1 - LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE)\n    : withFirstInsurance;\n  return roundInMhpcoFavorForPremium(withLoyalty + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  const results: StepResult[] = scenario.steps.map((step) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const premium = calculateQuotePremium(\n        scenario.customer,\n        step.items as ItemInput[],\n      );\n      return { premium };\n    }\n    return { payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 };\n  });\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784911767728},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed green, includes the earlier empty-list test still passing. Continuing