putes an item's premium including *both* a curse surcharge AND a high-enchantment surcharge (added in this cycle)\n- **Question**: Does \"WithCurseModifier\" clearly describe what the function actually does now?\n- **Assessment**: No — the name is now stale. It mentions only the curse modifier, but the function also applies the high-enchantment surcharge. A reader would reasonably expect this function to *not* touch enchantment logic, which is misleading.\n- **Decision**: Rename to `calculateItemPremiumWithSurcharges` — generic enough to cover both current surcharges (curse, high-enchantment) and any future ones (e.g., dragon-material), without needing another rename each time a new surcharge is added.\n\n## Initial APP Mass (target function, pre-refactor)\n\n```ts\nconst calculateItemPremiumWithCurseModifier = (item: ItemInput): number => {\n  const itemBase = MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? itemBase * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const highEnchantmentSurcharge =\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? itemBase * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return itemBase + curseSurcharge + highEnchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n```\n\n- Bindings: `item`, `itemBase`, `curseSurcharge`, `highEnchantmentSurcharge` = 4\n- Constants: `0` (×2, ?? fallbacks) = 2\n- Invocations: property/index access treated as negligible; `??` (×2) = 2 (informal)\n- Conditionals: ternary ×2 = 8\n- Assignments: `const` bindings not counted as mutation-assignments (they're bindings) = 0\n\nTotal Mass ≈ **1(binding item) + 3(other bindings) + 2(constants) + 8(conditionals) = 14**\n\n## Simple Design Rule Evaluation\n\n1. **Tests Pass**: All 10 passing before refactor — confirmed.\n2. **Reveals Intent**: Name was stale (see above) → **renamed**.\n3. **No Duplication**: The two surcharge computations follow the same shape (`condition ? base * rate : 0`) but each has distinct semantics (cursed flag vs. enchantment threshold) — extracting a generic \"surcharge applier\" helper would reduce clarity for two cases and isn't justified yet (would only pay off with a 3rd+ surcharge, e.g., dragon-material, coming later). Kept as-is per Rule 2 > Rule 3.\n4. **Fewest Elements**: Structure (base + surcharge + surcharge) is already minimal for two independent additive modifiers — no unnecessary elements found.\n\n## APP Mass After Refactor\n\nFunction body is unchanged (only the identifier changed), so mass is unchanged: **14** (rename doesn't affect mass — it's a Rule 2 improvement, not an APP-driven one).\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n- **Naming**: Renamed `calculateItemPremiumWithCurseModifier` → `calculateItemPremiumWithSurcharges` at both definition and call site, so the name accurately reflects that the function now applies multiple surcharge types (curse + high-enchantment), not just curse.\n- **Mass**: Unchanged (14 → 14) — this was a clarity fix, not a structural change.\n- **Duplication/Elements**: Evaluated, no changes needed — current structure is appropriately minimal for two independent surcharges.\n\nTests: `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` → **10 passed, 25 todo** (all green, unchanged from before refactor)."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":29035,"output":1387,"cacheRead":10086,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":40508,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784911855792,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-7a4e580c-532f-4b9d-808f-42d80002e95d","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":98265,"output":7142,"cacheRead":59526,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":40508,"turns":6},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784911869919},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_0197f6dKuZsVufzC5qoVvUAd","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experim