` = 4\n- Invocations: `reduce`, `Math.max`, `-` (arithmetic not counted as invocation) = 2\n- Conditionals: 0\n- Loops: 1 (reduce)\n- Assignments: 0 (const declarations, not mutations)\n\nTotal Mass ≈ 3 + 4 + 4 (2×2) + 0 + 5 + 0 = 16\n\n**Refactored Code Mass** (after extraction):\n```ts\nconst calculateClaimPayout = (damages: Damage[]): number =>\n  damages.reduce(\n    (total, damage) => total + Math.max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE_PER_DAMAGE),\n    0,\n  );\n...\nconst damages = (step.incident as { damages: Damage[] }).damages;\nconst payout = calculateClaimPayout(damages);\nreturn { payout, remainingCap: 0 };\n```\n- Call-site mass: Constants (`DEDUCTIBLE_PER_DAMAGE`=1, `0`=1) bindings (`damages`, `payout`) = 2, invocation (`calculateClaimPayout`) = 2, loop moved into helper.\n- Total mass is unchanged in absolute terms (logic just moved), but call-site mass in `runScenario` drops from 16 to ~5, since the loop/conditional-free arithmetic now lives in a named, single-purpose function.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Extracted the inline damage-summation logic into `calculateClaimPayout(damages: Damage[]): number`, matching the existing `calculateQuotePremium` naming/structure pattern.\n- Added an exported `Damage` interface to replace the ad-hoc inline cast type `{ damages: { amount: number }[] }`, removing type duplication and improving readability of the cast in `runScenario`.\n- `runScenario` is now a clean dispatcher: each branch delegates to a single well-named calculation function (`calculateQuotePremium` / `calculateClaimPayout`), improving Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) and Rule 3 (removes structural/type duplication between the two branches).\n\n**Mass Change**: `runScenario`'s claim branch mass reduced from ~16 to ~5 at the call site (logic relocated into a dedicated, testable, well-named function rather than eliminated — appropriate since Rule 2 clarity took priority over pure mass reduction).\n\n**Tests**: All 12 passing tests remain green (`NODE_ENV=development pnpm test`)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 12\nRecent Green phase: Added claim-step handling in runScenario: sums each damage entry's amount minus a 100G deductible (floored at 0 with Math.max), returns {payout, remainingCap: 0} (remainingCap still stubbed at 0).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Note: run tests with `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` since NODE_ENV=production is set in the environment by default and prevents vitest devDependency install/run.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 12\nRecent Green phase: Added claim-step handling in runScenario: sums each damage entry's amount minus a 100G deductible (floored at 0 with Math.max), returns {payout, remainingCap: 0} (remainingCap still stubbed at 0).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Note: run tests with `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` since NODE_ENV=production is set in the environment by default and prevents vitest devDependency install/run.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784911924674},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01X9PnASGJ9p1Q9vputCRdRZ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01421XTuUxcnNEy3dwNVvpMA","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":289,"output":243,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10288,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784911924694,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-f995a36a-73e4-4498-b327-e6bb222a8972","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01X9PnASGJ9p1Q9vputCRdRZ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: unknown[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: unknown;\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport type StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nexport interface ScenarioResult {\n  results: StepResult[];\n}\n\nexport interface ItemInput {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM = 25;\nconst BLOCK_OF_THREE_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nexport const calculateItemsBasePremium = (items: ItemInput[]): number => {\n  const countsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    countsByType.set(item.type, (countsByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n\n  return Array.from(countsByType.values()).reduce(\n    (total, count) =>\n      total +\n      (count === 3 ? BLOCK_OF_THREE_PREMIUM : count * BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM),\n    0,\n  );\n};\n\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\nconst calculateItemPremiumWithSurcharges = (item: ItemInput): number => {\n  const itemBase = MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? itemBase * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const highEnchantmentSurcharge =\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? itemBase * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return itemBase + curseSurcharge + highEnchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nexport const calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers = (\n  items: ItemInput[],\n): number => {\n  return items.reduce(\n    (total, item) => total + calculateItemPremiumWithSurcharges(item),\n    0,\n  );\n};\n\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst roundInMhpcoFavorForPremium = (amount: number): number =>\n  Math.ceil(amount);\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: ItemInput[],\n): number => {\n  const policyBase = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance =\n    policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const isLongStanding = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n  const withLoyalty = isLongStanding\n    ? withFirstInsurance * (1 - LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE)\n    : withFirstInsurance;\n  return roundInMhpcoFavorForPremium(withLoyalty + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE_PER_DAMAGE = 100;\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  const results: StepResult[] = scenario.steps.map((step) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const premium = calculateQuotePremium(\n        scenario.customer,\n        step.items as ItemInput[],\n      );\n      return { premium };\n    }\n    const damages = (step.incident as { damages: { amount: number }[] })\n      .damages;\n    const payout = damages.reduce(\n      (total, damage) =>\n        total + Math.max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE_PER_DAMAGE),\n      0,\n    );\n    return { payout, remainingCap: 0 };\n  });\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784911927029},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01421XTuUxcnNEy3dwNVvpMA","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  runScenario,\n  calculateItemsBasePremium,\n  calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers,\n} from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Simplest cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums for main items (no modifiers, established customer to avoid first-insurance surcharge complexity is NOT possible per spec: every item is first insurance regardless -- so we always get the +10% surcharge unless combined with other rules explicitly shown in the spec) ---\n  // NOTE: Per spec, every item in a quote is treated as first insurance, so a single-item\n  // quote with a newcomer customer (0 years, first quote) always includes the 10% first\n  // insurance surcharge. We use the \"Newcomer with a cursed sword\" example directly, and\n  // build up isolated base-premium tests using multi-item policies where the spec gives us\n  // a clean base-premium number before modifiers (as in \"Modifier scope on multi-item policies\").\n\n  // --- Building block of 3 alike components ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> base premium 50 G (no block)\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(50);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> base premium 60 G (block applies)\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> base premium 100 G (no block -- block requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> base premium 175 G\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(175);\n  });\n\n  // --- \"Alike\" components ---\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> base premium 75 G (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(75);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> base premium 120 G (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(120);\n  });\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it(\"policy with cursed sword (100 G base) + plain amulet (60 G base) -> curse surcharge applies only to cursed item's base premium (160 G base + 50 G curse = 210 G before further modifiers and fee)\", () => {\n    const result = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", cursed: true },\n      { type: \"amulet\", cursed: false },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(210);\n  });\n\n  // --- Modifier thresholds ---\n  it(\"customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> loyalty discount applies\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // policyBasePremium = 60; +10% first insurance = 66; -20% loyalty = 52.8;\n    // 52.8 + 5 fee = 57.8, rounded up in MHPCO's favor = 58\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 58 });\n  });\n  it(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies; if cursed, both surcharges apply\", () => {\n    const highEnchantedOnly = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 },\n    ]);\n    const highEnchantedAndCursed = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true },\n    ]);\n    // sword base 100; +30% high enchantment = 130\n    expect(highEnchantedOnly).toBe(130);\n    // sword base 100; +30% high enchantment + 50% curse = 100 + 30 + 50 = 180\n    expect(highEnchantedAndCursed).toBe(180);\n  });\n  it(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge; curse surcharge applies only if cursed\", () => {\n    const plain = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4 },\n    ]);\n    const cursed = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4, cursed: true },\n    ]);\n    expect(plain).toBe(100);\n    expect(cursed).toBe(150);\n  });\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword with exactly enchantment 8, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (high-enchantment clause applies, then deductible)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Deductible per damage event ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon attack damages an insured sword (500 G) and an insured amulet (300 G) -> payout 600 G (100 G deductible applies once per damaged item)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Standard reimbursement (no special clauses) ---\n  it(\"regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G -> payout 400 G (full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible; no special clause applies)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toMatchObject({ payout: 400 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\n    \"damage to a rune (insurance value 250 G), damage 200 G -> payout 100 G (full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible; runes have no enchantment/material special clause)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Enchantment threshold vs. dragon material ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (both clauses apply; 50% rule wins, then deductible: 500 - 100)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G -> payout 700 G (only dragon-material clause: full reimbursement, then deductible: 800 - 100)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (only high-enchantment clause: 50% first, then deductible: 500 - 100)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Multiple items of the same type ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy covers two swords -> insurance sum 2000 G (= 2x1000), cap 4000 G\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon attack damages both swords; damages array has two {itemType: 'sword', ...} entries -> each entry treated as separate damage with its own deductible\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"damages array has more entries of a given type than policy covers (two sword damages but only one sword insured) -> CLI exits with non-zero status code; whole claim is rejected\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Cap exhaustion ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy covers a sword and an amulet -> insurance sum 1600 G (= 1000 + 600), cap 3200 G\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"cursed sword (insurance value 1000 G, premium with modifiers 165 G) -> cap 2000 G (based on unmodified insurance value; premium modifiers do not raise the cap)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy covers a sword and 3 runes (a block) -> insurance sum 1750 G (= 1000 + 3x250); block discount affects premium only, not insurance sum\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"sword insured (insurance sum 1000 G, cap 2000 G); two successive claims of 1500 G each -> first claim payout 1400 G, cap remaining 600 G\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"second successive claim of 1500 G after first -> payout 600 G, cap remaining 0 G (desired 1400 G reduced to remaining cap)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Rounding in the MHPCO's favor ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"premium calculation yielding 197.5 G -> final premium 198 G (rounded up)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"payout calculation yielding 350.5 G -> final payout 350 G (rounded down)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Edge cases ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"quote includes an item with an unknown type (e.g. 'broomstick') -> CLI exits with non-zero status code and writes error to stderr; no results written to stdout\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"claim references a damage entry whose item is not part of the policy (e.g. amulet damaged when only a sword is insured) -> CLI exits with non-zero status code and writes error to stderr\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"claim references a damage entry with an unknown item type -> CLI exits with non-zero status code and writes error to stderr\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"claim contains a damage entry with amount: -200 -> CLI exits with non-zero status code and writes error to stderr\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Integration examples ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"newcomer with a cursed sword (steel, enchantment 3), 0 years, no previous contract -> premium 165 G (100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance = 160 + 5 fee = 165)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"long-standing customer's (3 years) second quote in scenario, cursed sword (steel, enchantment 7) -> premium 160 G (100 base + 50 curse + 30 high enchantment - 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance - 15 follow-up = 155 + 5 fee = 160); first insurance surcharge still applies per item regardless of customer history\"\n  );\n\n  // --- CLI-level schema example ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"CLI schema example: amulet quote then claim -> stdout results array matches shape {premium} then {payout, remainingCap}\"\n  );\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784911927029},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01HAK4YKiHzEY1Mc1br8BEf4","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && NODE_ENV=development pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":6214,"output":160,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":16130,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784911927030,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-37747aa0-b83d-47bb-9a2a-b6870ff6721d","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01HAK4YKiHzEY1Mc1br8BEf4","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (35 tests | 23 skipped) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  12 passed | 23 todo (35)\n   Start at  16:52:10\n   Duration  157ms (transform 32ms, setup 0ms, collect 31ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 42ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784911930228},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01VdfChE9gskYCCrJ6efY8LX","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/