00, potion 400) and COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE (250, fallback for runes/moonstones/etc). Added getItemInsuranceValue, calculateInsuranceSum (sums insurance values across policy items), and PAYOUT_CAP_MULTIPLIER (2). runScenario now computes cap = calculateInsuranceSum(policyItems) * 2 and returns remainingCap = cap - payout for each claim.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Note: run tests with `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` since NODE_ENV=production is set in the environment by default and prevents vitest devDependency install/run.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":1584,"output":633,"cacheRead":110187,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":112404,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784912250232,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-2b4709f4-0eec-48f2-81de-ff85a6f2f7e6","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_013RRWUktA2MuPWRv28AWctu","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Naming Evaluation\n\n**Current names**: `getItemInsuranceValue`, `calculateInsuranceSum`, `MAIN_ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES`/`MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS` (before refactor)\n\n- `getItemInsuranceValue`: Clearly reveals intent — retrieves the insurance value for an item. Kept as-is.\n- `calculateInsuranceSum`: Clearly reveals intent — sums insurance values over a policy's items. Kept as-is.\n- `MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS` and `MAIN_ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES`: These were two **parallel lookup tables keyed by the exact same set of item types** (sword, amulet, staff, potion), representing two facets of one concept: \"main item configuration.\" Having them as separate maps obscured that `sword`'s base premium (100) and insurance value (1000) are properties of the *same* conceptual entity.\n\nDecision: **Merge into a single `MAIN_ITEM_CONFIG` map** of `{ basePremium, insuranceValue }` per item type, accessed via one lookup function `getMainItemConfig`. This better reveals intent — \"here is everything the system knows about a main item type\" — rather than two independently-named, coincidentally-parallel tables.\n\n## APP Mass Calculation\n\n**Before** (two separate lookup tables + two fallback constants + two accessor functions):\n```ts\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = { sword: 100, amulet: 60, staff: 80, potion: 40 };\n// calculateItemPremiumWithSurcharges: MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0\nconst MAIN_ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = { sword: 1000, amulet: 600, staff: 800, potion: 400 };\nconst COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE = 250;\nconst getItemInsuranceValue = (item) => MAIN_ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type] ?? COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE;\n```\n- Constants: 8 (map literals) + 1 (250) + 1 (0 fallback) = 10\n- Bindings: 2 (map names) + 1 (COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE) + 1 (getItemInsuranceValue param `item`) = 4\n- Invocations: 2 (property lookups `[item.type]` in each) = 4\n- Conditionals: 2 (`??` fallbacks) x4 = 8\n- Assignments: 0\n- **Subtotal for this concern: ~26**\n\n**After** (one merged config map + one accessor):\n```ts\nconst MAIN_ITEM_CONFIG: Record<string, MainItemConfig> = {\n  sword: { basePremium: 100, insuranceValue: 1000 },\n  amulet: { basePremium: 60, insuranceValue: 600 },\n  staff: { basePremium: 80, insuranceValue: 800 },\n  potion: { basePremium: 40, insuranceValue: 400 },\n};\nconst COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE = 250;\nconst DEFAULT_MAIN_ITEM_CONFIG: MainItemConfig = { basePremium: 0, insuranceValue: COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE };\nconst getMainItemConfig = (type) => MAIN_ITEM_CONFIG[type] ?? DEFAULT_MAIN_ITEM_CONFIG;\n```\n- Constants: 8 (nested literals) + 1 (250) + 1 (0) = 10\n- Bindings: 1 (MAIN_ITEM_CONFIG) + 1 (COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE) + 1 (DEFAULT_MAIN_ITEM_CONFIG) + 1 (param `type`) = 4\n- Invocations: 1 (single lookup, called from both `calculateItemPremiumWithSurcharges` and `getItemInsuranceValue`, each -2) = 2 (lookup itself)\n- Conditionals: 1 (`??`) x4 = 4\n- Assignments: 0\n- **Subtotal for this concern: ~20**\n\nCallers (`calculateItemPremiumWithSurcharges`, `getItemInsuranceValue`) now each do one field access (`.basePremium` / `.insuranceValue`) instead of a full map lookup with fallback — duplication of \"which types count as main items\" and their fallback logic is eliminated (was previously encoded twice).\n\n**Mass change: ~26 → ~20 (delta -6)**, with the larger benefit being **Rule 3 (DRY)**: one source of truth for \"what is a main item,\" instead of two maps that must be kept in sync by convention.\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Unified two coincidentally-parallel per-type maps into one `MAIN_ITEM_CONFIG` record, making explicit that base premium and insurance value are properties of the same conceptual \"main item\" entity.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Removed the duplicated notion of \"the set of main item types\" (previously implicit in two separately-maintained maps with independent fallback constants).\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: One lookup function (`getMainItemConfig`) now serves both premium and insurance-value calculations, replacing two separate accessor functions.\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n**Refactoring**: Merged `MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS` and `MAIN_ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES` into a single `MAIN_ITEM_CONFIG` lookup table with a `getMainItemConfig` accessor, eliminating duplicated per-type-map maintenance.\n**Mass Change**: ~26 → ~20 (delta -6) for the affected lookup logic.\n**Tests**: All 19 passing tests remain green (verified via `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test`)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-18-07_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 19\nRecent Green phase: Added MAIN_ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES lookup (sword 1000, amulet 600, staff 800, potion 400) and COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE (250, fallback for runes/moonstones/etc). Added getItemInsuranceValue, calculateInsuranceSum (sums insurance values across policy items), and PAYOUT_CAP_MULTIPLIER (2). runScenario now computes cap = calculateInsuranceSum(policyItems) * 2 and returns remainingCap = cap - payout for each claim.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Note: run tests with `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` since NODE_ENV=production is set in the environment by default and prevents vitest devDependency install/run.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 19\nRecent Green phase: Added MAIN_ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES lookup (sword 1000, amulet 600, staff 800, potion 400) and COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE (250, fallback for runes/moonstones/etc). Added getItemInsuranceValue, calculateInsuranceSum (sums insurance values across policy items), and PAYOUT_CAP_MULTIPLIER (2). runScenario now computes cap = calculateInsuranceSum(policyItems) * 2 and returns remainingCap = cap - payout for each claim.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Note: run tests with `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` since NODE_ENV=production is set in the environment by default and prevents vitest devDependency install/run.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784912257096},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01WQnoxCAXRWFF5AVYHEvAg7","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01JuyMY7SPJmqExWpgGNMRvG","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":406,"output":130,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10292,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784912257121,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-098567fe-364d-42c1-8c93-9d15c7e00fe9","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01WQnoxCAXRWFF5AVYHEvAg7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: unknown[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: unknown;\n}\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport type StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nexport interface ScenarioResult {\n  results: StepResult[];\n}\n\nexport interface ItemInput {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM = 25;\nconst BLOCK_OF_THREE_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nexport const calculateItemsBasePremium = (items: ItemInput[]): number => {\n  const countsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    countsByType.set(item.type, (countsByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n\n  return Array.from(countsByType.values()).reduce(\n    (total, count) =>\n      total +\n      (count === 3 ? BLOCK_OF_THREE_PREMIUM : count * BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM),\n    0,\n  );\n};\n\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\nconst calculateItemPremiumWithSurcharges = (item: ItemInput): number => {\n  const itemBase = MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? itemBase * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const highEnchantmentSurcharge =\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? itemBase * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return itemBase + curseSurcharge + highEnchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nexport const calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers = (\n  items: ItemInput[],\n): number => {\n  return items.reduce(\n    (total, item) => total + calculateItemPremiumWithSurcharges(item),\n    0,\n  );\n};\n\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst roundInMhpcoFavorForPremium = (amount: number): number =>\n  Math.ceil(amount);\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: ItemInput[],\n): number => {\n  const policyBase = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance =\n    policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const isLongStanding = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n  const withLoyalty = isLongStanding\n    ? withFirstInsurance * (1 - LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE)\n    : withFirstInsurance;\n  return roundInMhpcoFavorForPremium(withLoyalty + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE_PER_DAMAGE = 100;\nconst DAMAGE_HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst DAMAGE_HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\nconst FULL_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 1;\n\nconst calculateReimbursementRate = (item: ItemInput | undefined): number => {\n  if ((item?.enchantment ?? 0) >= DAMAGE_HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    return DAMAGE_HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return FULL_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n};\n\nconst calculateClaimPayout = (\n  damages: Damage[],\n  policyItems: ItemInput[],\n): number =>\n  damages.reduce((total, damage) => {\n    const item = policyItems.find(\n      (policyItem) => policyItem.type === damage.itemType,\n    );\n    const reimbursementRate = calculateReimbursementRate(item);\n    const reimbursed = damage.amount * reimbursementRate;\n    return total + Math.max(0, reimbursed - DEDUCTIBLE_PER_DAMAGE);\n  }, 0);\n\nconst MAIN_ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE = 250;\n\nconst getItemInsuranceValue = (item: ItemInput): number =>\n  MAIN_ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type] ?? COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE;\n\nconst calculateInsuranceSum = (items: ItemInput[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((total, item) => total + getItemInsuranceValue(item), 0);\n\nconst PAYOUT_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  const policiesByStepIndex = new Map<number, ItemInput[]>();\n  const results: StepResult[] = scenario.steps.map((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items as ItemInput[];\n      policiesByStepIndex.set(index, items);\n      const premium = calculateQuotePremium(scenario.customer, items);\n      return { premium };\n    }\n    const policyItems = policiesByStepIndex.get(step.policy) ?? [];\n    const damages = (step.incident as { damages: Damage[] }).damages;\n    const payout = calculateClaimPayout(damages, policyItems);\n    const cap =\n      calculateInsuranceSum(policyItems) * PAYOUT_CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n    return { payout, remainingCap: cap - payout };\n  });\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784912260469},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01JuyMY7SPJmqExWpgGNMRvG","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  runScenario,\n  calculateItemsBasePremium,\n  calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers,\n} from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Simplest cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums for main items (no modifiers, established customer to avoid first-insurance surcharge complexity is NOT possible per spec: every item is first insurance regardless -- so we always get the +10% surcharge unless combined with other rules explicitly shown in the spec) ---\n  // NOTE: Per spec, every item in a quote is treated as first insurance, so a single-item\n  // quote with a newcomer customer (0 years, first quote) always includes the 10% first\n  // insurance surcharge. We use the \"Newcomer with a cursed sword\" example directly, and\n  // build up isolated base-premium tests using multi-item policies where the spec gives us\n  // a clean base-premium number before modifiers (as in \"Modifier scope on multi-item policies\").\n\n  // --- Building block of 3 alike components ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> base premium 50 G (no block)\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(50);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> base premium 60 G (block applies)\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> base premium 100 G (no block -- block requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> base premium 175 G\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(175);\n  });\n\n  // --- \"Alike\" components ---\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> base premium 75 G (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(75);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> base premium 120 G (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const base = calculateItemsBasePremium([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(base).toBe(120);\n  });\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it(\"policy with cursed sword (100 G base) + plain amulet (60 G base) -> curse surcharge applies only to cursed item's base premium (160 G base + 50 G curse = 210 G before further modifiers and fee)\", () => {\n    const result = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", cursed: true },\n      { type: \"amulet\", cursed: false },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(210);\n  });\n\n  // --- Modifier thresholds ---\n  it(\"customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> loyalty discount applies\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // policyBasePremium = 60; +10% first insurance = 66; -20% loyalty = 52.8;\n    // 52.8 + 5 fee = 57.8, rounded up in MHPCO's favor = 58\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 58 });\n  });\n  it(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies; if cursed, both surcharges apply\", () => {\n    const highEnchantedOnly = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 },\n    ]);\n    const highEnchantedAndCursed = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true },\n    ]);\n    // sword base 100; +30% high enchantment = 130\n    expect(highEnchantedOnly).toBe(130);\n    // sword base 100; +30% high enchantment + 50% curse = 100 + 30 + 50 = 180\n    expect(highEnchantedAndCursed).toBe(180);\n  });\n  it(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge; curse surcharge applies only if cursed\", () => {\n    const plain = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4 },\n    ]);\n    const cursed = calculatePolicyBasePremiumWithItemModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4, cursed: true },\n    ]);\n    expect(plain).toBe(100);\n    expect(cursed).toBe(150);\n  });\n  it(\"dragon-material sword with exactly enchantment 8, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (high-enchantment clause applies, then deductible)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 8 }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toMatchObject({ payout: 400 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Deductible per damage event ---\n  it(\"dragon attack damages an insured sword (500 G) and an insured amulet (300 G) -> payout 600 G (the 100 G deductible applies once per damaged item)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [\n              { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n              { itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 300 },\n            ],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toMatchObject({ payout: 600 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Standard reimbursement (no special clauses) ---\n  it(\"regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G -> payout 400 G (full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible; no special clause applies)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toMatchObject({ payout: 400 });\n  });\n  it(\"damage to a rune (insurance value 250 G), damage 200 G -> payout 100 G (full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible; runes have no enchantment/material special clause)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toMatchObject({ payout: 100 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Enchantment threshold vs. dragon material ---\n  it(\"dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (both clauses apply; the 50% rule wins, then deductible: 500 - 100)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9 }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toMatchObject({ payout: 400 });\n  });\n  it(\"dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G -> payout 700 G (only dragon-material clause: full reimbursement, then deductible: 800 - 100)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5 }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toMatchObject({ payout: 700 });\n  });\n  it(\"steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (only high-enchantment clause: 50% first, then deductible: 500 - 100)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9 }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toMatchObject({ payout: 400 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Multiple items of the same type ---\n  it(\"policy covers two swords -> insurance sum 2000 G (= 2x1000), cap 4000 G\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // payout = 500 - 100 = 400; cap = 4000; remainingCap = 4000 - 400 = 3600\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 400, remainingCap: 3600 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon attack damages both swords; damages array has two {itemType: 'sword', ...} entries -> each entry treated as separate damage with its own deductible\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"damages array has more entries of a given type than policy covers (two sword damages but only one sword insured) -> CLI exits with non-zero status code; whole claim is rejected\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Cap exhaustion ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy covers a sword and an amulet -> insurance sum 1600 G (= 1000 + 600), cap 3200 G\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"cursed sword (insurance value 1000 G, premium with modifiers 165 G) -> cap 2000 G (based on unmodified insurance value; premium modifiers do not raise the cap)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy covers a sword and 3 runes (a block) -> insurance sum 1750 G (= 1000 + 3x250); block discount affects premium only, not insurance sum\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"sword insured (insurance sum 1000 G, cap 2000 G); two successive claims of 1500 G each -> first claim payout 1400 G, cap remaining 600 G\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"second successive claim of 1500 G after first -> payout 600 G, cap remaining 0 G (desired 1400 G reduced to remaining cap)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Rounding in the MHPCO's favor ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"premium calculation yielding 197.5 G -> final premium 198 G (rounded up)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"payout calculation yielding 350.5 G -> final payout 350 G (rounded down)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Edge cases ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"quote includes an item with an unknown type (e