dings: `quoteStepCount` (decl), `isFollowUpContract` = 2\n- Invocations: 0 (no calls here)\n- Conditionals: 0 (the `>` comparison isn't a branch itself, counted as part of assignment expression — no separate conditional)\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: `let quoteStepCount = 0` (1) + `quoteStepCount += 1` (1) + `isFollowUpContract = ...` (1) = 3\n\nTotal Mass: 2(1) + 2(1) + 0 + 0 + 0 + 3(6) = 2 + 2 + 18 = **22**\n\n## Apply Simple Design Rules\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass)**: All 34 tests currently green. ✓ baseline confirmed.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: `quoteStepCount` is a mutable counter mixing \"count\" semantics with a boolean need. Renaming/restructuring to a boolean flag with `let` reveals intent more directly: \"has a quote already happened.\"\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: No duplication found in this area.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: The counter and its `+=` mutation are more machinery than needed — a single boolean flag flip is simpler.\n\nI'll refactor: replace the counter with a boolean flag `hasPriorQuote`, removing the unnecessary increment/comparison, and flipping it right after use."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01AmFCRuP3TScAnsjJh2Pdmd","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"  const policyStateByIndex = new Map<number, PolicyState>();\n  let quoteStepCount = 0;\n  const results: StepResult[] = scenario.steps.map((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items as ItemInput[];\n      const isFollowUpContract = quoteStepCount > 0;\n      quoteStepCount += 1;","newText":"  const policyStateByIndex = new Map<number, PolicyState>();\n  let hasPriorQuote = false;\n  const results: StepResult[] = scenario.steps.map((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items as ItemInput[];\n      const isFollowUpContract = hasPriorQuote;\n      hasPriorQuote = true;"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonn